From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kai Ninomiya <kainino@chromium.org>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 12:44:58 -0700
Subject: Add round_up_3d_texture_size_to_pot_for_limit workaround for PowerVR

PowerVR drivers have an issue which seems to be specific to 3D textures
where they round up NPOT sizes to POT sizes before doing some size math.

Just do this for all PowerVR drivers because we don't know the driver
version where it's fixed, and this workaround is only for the validating
command decoder.

Bug: 551673541
Change-Id: Ia6fe56f84ada7f91942253211f3156718e71dc6b
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8421322
Reviewed-by: Kenneth Russell <kbr@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Kai Ninomiya <kainino@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Geoff Lang <geofflang@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1700049}

